Name: Satanel.
Age: 1200+.
Species: Demon.
Status: Alive.
Affiliation: mostly himself or who he chooses to cooperate with, which are rare occurrence.
Title/Nickname: The Death of All Things, Demon of Morality, The Adversary of All Living Things, Pray Slaughter, Demon who cannot kill.
Class: Mage. 
Rank: Greater Demon.
Alignment: Chaotic Neutral.
Gender: Male.
Height/Weight: 6’4 ”/180 lbs.
Eye Color: Red.
Hair Color: Red.

Appearance: Satanel possesses the imposing appearance of a tall, slender yet powerfully built young man, with a physique that combines lean muscular definition, broad shoulders, and an almost statuesque elegance. His exposed upper body reveals a well-developed chest, pronounced collarbones, and sharply defined musculature, while his skin bears an unnatural, dark charcoal-gray complexion that contrasts dramatically with the pale garments enveloping him. His face is strikingly handsome yet deeply unsettling, characterized by sharp, angular features, a narrow jawline, a straight nose, and thin lips that rest in a faint, enigmatic smile, giving him an expression of cold amusement, quiet arrogance, and absolute composure. His long, wild crimson-red hair falls in thick, uneven, sharply pointed strands around his head, extending past his shoulders in places, with heavy, disheveled bangs cascading over most of his face and obscuring much of his eyes. The hair possesses a vivid blood-red coloration with darker scarlet and black undertones, creating a striking contrast against his shadowed features. Beneath the tangled fringe, a single partially visible eye glimmers with an ominous reddish-orange light, its piercing gaze suggesting an unnerving awareness despite the apparent concealment of his expression. Dark shadows gather around his eyes, cheekbones, and neck, lending his countenance an almost corpse-like severity, while the subtle upward curve of his mouth suggests a restrained, knowing smirk rather than genuine warmth. His attire consists of an elaborate arrangement of flowing, ivory-white ceremonial robes that resemble a combination of ancient priestly vestments, sacred burial garments, and the draped clothing of a mythological deity. The fabric is extraordinarily voluminous, wrapping loosely around his torso and cascading downward in numerous overlapping layers, with broad folds, sweeping edges, and long, irregular strips that appear to move independently in an unseen current. A thick, scarf-like mantle of white cloth encircles his shoulders and neck, forming a substantial, loosely gathered collar before extending outward into enormous, ribbon-like lengths of fabric. One particularly prominent extension streams horizontally from his right shoulder before curling downward, creating the impression of a supernatural garment suspended in perpetual motion. His chest remains partially exposed through the deep opening of the robe, revealing the upper portion of his muscular torso and an intricate crimson-red circular marking situated around the lower sternum and upper abdomen. This marking resembles a mystical seal or occult insignia, composed of concentric curved patterns, dark geometric details, and densely arranged symbols, its blood-red coloration standing out sharply against his dark skin. The robe gathers around his waist in an elaborate knot, from which numerous overlapping lengths of fabric descend toward the ground, forming a long, flowing lower garment that conceals most of his legs. The material alternates between brilliant ivory-white and muted gray-beige tones, with areas of intricate, honeycomb-like or hexagonal patterning visible across the inner surfaces and shaded folds. Thick black outlines and irregular patches of darkness accentuate the garment's layered construction, while several of its lower edges appear torn, fragmented, or dissolved into jagged, shadow-like shapes. The hem spreads outward around his feet in a chaotic arrangement of trailing cloth, with narrow strips twisting and curling across the ground. Beneath the cascading robes, small portions of his dark legs are visible, although his footwear remains largely concealed by the surrounding fabric. Perhaps his most distinctive physical feature is the presence of two enormous, pale serpents that coil around his body, their elongated forms appearing almost inseparable from the flowing garments. Their bodies possess ivory-white and pale gray scales, individually outlined in darker tones, producing an intricate overlapping pattern that catches the light along their curved surfaces. One serpent rises from the lower left side of his figure, its thick body sweeping upward in a broad arc before curving inward toward his waist, where its narrow, angular head emerges from the folds of his clothing. The second serpent extends from the right side, its long body forming an immense elevated curve before descending toward the center of his lower torso. Both serpents possess elongated, wedge-shaped heads, small dark eyes, finely defined scales, and closed mouths, giving them an eerily tranquil appearance despite their immense size. Their movements appear graceful and deliberate, with their bodies weaving through the trailing cloth in such a way that the distinction between living serpent and supernatural garment becomes visually ambiguous. The serpents' pale coloration mirrors the robes almost perfectly, reinforcing the impression that they are extensions of his presence rather than ordinary creatures accompanying him. His arms are largely concealed beneath the sweeping fabric, with the garment's enormous sleeves and trailing folds obscuring the exact positioning of his hands. His posture is upright, relaxed, and utterly unguarded, with his shoulders slightly lowered and his head inclined forward just enough for his crimson bangs to cast his expression into deeper shadow. Despite the extravagant movement of the clothing and the serpents surrounding him, his central figure remains remarkably still, creating a powerful contrast between his motionless composure and the restless, almost living forms encircling him. His overall silhouette is elongated and imposing, narrow at the head and upper torso before expanding dramatically outward through the massive flowing robes and serpentine coils. The combination of blood-red hair, charcoal-gray skin, ivory ceremonial garments, crimson occult markings, and gigantic white serpents gives him an appearance that is simultaneously divine, sinister, majestic, and profoundly inhuman. He resembles an ancient serpentine divinity or forbidden god clothed in sacred vestments, possessing an unsettling beauty that derives not from ornamentation or conventional grandeur, but from the extraordinary contrast between his serene expression and the monstrous, supernatural imagery surrounding him.

Personality: Despite his appearance, Satanel has an enigmatic, grim, cold, mean, heartless, cynical, solitary, merciless, and highly brooding personality, appearing to care about nothing but surprisingly has an unexpected human reaction and very rare smile not because he can conceals it but the threshold for him to express them is extremely high. He has no interest in harming anyone so long they have no concern in harming him except for demons not because he kills him seamlessly but because they keep on crossing that threshold that causes him to retaliate. However, Satanel harbors a deep hatred and resentment for demons and himself due to his self-awareness of his demonic nature and excluded himself from ordinary happiness even though he secretly wanted it. his sense of living is considered fractured and a constant sense of uncertainty on either he’s alive, and tried to gain the feeling of living through killing but couldn’t go through it with killing innocent people due to been given benevolent obstructions and decided Demons were a better fit since he felt less sense of guilt in doing it and yet couldn’t get any feeling out of it when he did numerous times and now prefers to kill on self-defence if necessary. Now stuck with that uncertainty of living, he listlessly continues to walk several miles without directions on a daily basis and gets lost constantly because his perception is extraordinary but his sense of direction simply isn't. That alone is abnormal, demons generally imitate human emotional expression without sharing humanity's underlying emotional experience.
Satanel, however, possesses genuine but exceptionally rare emotional reactions, self-loathing, moral restraint, and an unfulfilled desire for happiness. He isn't simply pretending to understand humanity. He is suffering from the uncertainty of whether he can truly experience life at all. Because magic reflects the nature of its wielder and Satanel's magic allows him to perceive the end of nearly everything around him, while his own existence remains something he cannot understand. Seven hundred years of living, and he still cannot decide what it means to be alive, and it’s a cruel irony. It’s also stated Satanel removed his horns and given Satanel's self-hatred, he might have tried to remove the most recognizable physical evidence of his demonic nature. And because Zeitsterben can irreversibly end a body part's existence, using it on his own horns would have very different implications from simply breaking them, and removing his horn would not make him human and he perhaps already knows that.

ABILITIES
Overall Power: Satanel is a nameless yet incredibly powerful demon who is regarded to comparable to Macht, the strongest among the Seven Sages of Destruction. According to Serie, Satanel had enough power to trace dead-point of entire kingdom to make the its entire structure collapse as well if he can perceive it. He was one of the few mages that defeated Frieren in the past, and spared her because she wasn’t a demon and Frieren in the present is still unable to imagine defeating him. Even the Greater Demon Solitär has stated that she is afraid to fight him knowing the result in inevitable death because of his “eyes.” He’s exceptional adaptability at deciphering and experience with seeing death  makes him extremely adaptable at deciphering complex deadlines, which why relying on defence spell against him are likely the least effective against when their defence have deadlines regardless of durability or refinement.

Immense Mana Output: As a Greater Demon who has lived for at least seven hundred years, Satanel possesses a colossal amount of mana. He states that he could fight Denken while countering Mistilziela for three days and three nights without any sign of fatigue. It’s considered Macht's and Satanel's mana levels are comparable.

Superhuman Strength and Speed: Satanel is an extremely powerful fighter with immense physical strength and speed, which fits well with his spell needing him to directly trace the deadlines. Despite being a mage, he usually prefers to fight with a longsword that he carries with him. His battle strength and agility are overwhelming enough to instantly wipe out a party of experienced demon fighters, including a first-class mage. He broke through Lernen's defensive magic with seemingly nothing but his physical strength when he had a hood on to conceal his identity. He’s considered fast enough to dodge lightning, and once noted to have instinctively dodged point blank Zoltraak from Frieren in the past when they first fought. It’s stated he fights more a killer then mage.

SPELL
Spell to Perceive the Death of All Creation — Zeitsterben: He possesses perception and visualisation capabilities detached from Life due to his uncertain sense of living that allows him see something normally considered impossible by living beings. Is it can be called a curse that opens up in the brain and eyes to allow Satanel to "perceive death" specifically the inherent "Death of an Existence" as visual signals in the form of Deadlines and Dead-Points. Although Satanel only sees the deadlines, certain deadlines act as the dead-points that Satanel would see in livings things. It is regarded as comparable curse to Macht, one that could not be dispelled even with the Magic of the Goddess. As a curse, it is imperceivable as magic and thus nearly impossible to defend against or heal against. Their usage is not entirely dependent on Satanel's physical eyes, as he can still "see" deadlines should he go blind or gouge his eyeballs out. "Death" is invisible to normal people, only accessed through perceiving the natural flaws with overly strong spiritual sight by looking through channels that normal people cannot perceive. These eyes seem the same "boundary" referred to in the "At The Boundary between Life and Death". In visualising to perceive death, it can be said he can see the Death itself. humans classify it as a curse rather than standard magic. It’s a curse is a form of magic that humans do not fundamentally understand. Because it operates outside conventional mana-based laws, it outputs zero detectable mana signature, bypasses any defensive magic barriers once traced, and cannot be dispelled by the magic of the Goddess and Satanel’s curse is considered-never before-precedented in history. The spell to perceive the death of a being or object depends entirely upon the Satanel's perception of death. Zeitsterben show the death of things, the weak points where everything is most easily broken and the imperfection in everything that will break down one day. Zeitsterben can be said to see the fate of all things, seeing the future, allowing him to see death. While there is a difference as to when a person or object will "end", it is certain that they will all arrive at that point because death is not something that "arrives", but rather is something already contained within an object at its creation and certainly bound to happen as part of the principle of causality. For these reasons, Zeitsterben can be considered the ultimate form of foresight. Anything with an origin must have an end, a "time of death" determined at the beginning, and as it already exists, it is not impossible to comprehend such a concept with the appropriate circuit in the eyes and brain, allowing them to be viewed as though a microscope. It is normal that cutting a living being's neck would kill them, their life stopping because it was cut, and conversely not being able to cut a being's neck would mean that they will not die. Zeitsterben can ignore the cause, instead allowing them to kill even that which is immune to all external effects. That which is cut falls apart and that which is "killed" becomes "dead", but rather than "tracing the deadlines causing the object to fall apart" and the object becoming dead because it was cut, it is "ending the lifespan and killing the object". It is the erasure of existence rather than physical destruction, so the object is "stopped" and the cut is the end result. When it comes to turning on and turning off, Satanel is able to shift his focal point to prevent himself from seeing the lines of death, returning his eyes to their regular appearance. Looking at the world as he normally would activates his spell, granting his eyes to change into a red hue. As opposed to the "physical phenomena that can be attained through modern technology", Zeitsterben are a "phenomenon that cannot be attained no matter what". By bypassing causality and the law of conservation of energy to actualize death.

Deadlines: Death emerges to the surface of an existence as Deadlines, and cutting along them will result in "Death", regardless of the constitution or properties of the object. The deadlines have no particular structure, so they can be described as solid, red "zigzagging scribbles" all over the world, even within the air itself, that look like cracks. They are harder to see during the day due to the light, but emit a sort of glow at night. The deadlines of a living organism will keep changing position as long as it is alive, and those Satanel perceives are constantly moving and irregular. The deadlines can be traced with any sort of object, effectively "breaking" the person or object along the line, cleanly cutting it without any need for force. The object tracing the lines "sinks into it", and although a finger will fit into the thicker parts, thinner objects like rulers or knives are more effective. While anything can be cut, Satanel has no say in where they can cut, as it depends on the placement of the lines of death. Serie theorizes that the deadlines are something like the weakest parts of the joints between molecules in an object or a predesignated switch within the genetic makeup that activates the death of the object. Those of Satanel are described as the "concept of longevity given form" rather than lines at which an "object can be easily cut apart". Completing a cut makes it impossible to heal under normal circumstances. The deadlines that are cut cause the corresponding part to die, making them never able to move again even if the main body is alive. While healing magic normally can heal an injury or a limb, they cannot regenerate an arm after Satanel cuts it off and is considered irreversible but it can be replaced by a prosthetic arm instead of restoring the one that was already gone. Beings will have different amounts of deadlines depending on their complexity. Humans will have a countable amount in geometric patterns. Demons have numerous lines all over their bodies that make their appearance hard to discern. Spirits will have very few "parts vulnerable to death".

Dead-Points: are from where all Deadlines seem to flow, resembling blood vessels. There can be a number of them on an object, and, whereas the Deadlines are "where things die easily", the Dead-Points are "death itself". The spell do not actually kill the "body", as the power of killing someone's life is very common in the world. The "points" seen by the eyes end the very meaning, the "existence", of whatever is "killed". The destruction, the extinguishing of life that comes afterward, is only a side effect of destroying their existence. Striking the point of death makes the entity completely cease to function. What "makes a living person a living person" or what "makes a hallway a hallway" is ended in the simplest way, unraveling its existence and making it no more. This makes it possible to kill the soul without harming the body, allowing for the destruction of one of two souls in a single body without the death of the other soul or the body itself. The weaker soul is the one that will be ended, so it is a battle of strength in that case. Dead-Points can be pierced by sharp objects. Piercing a Dead-Points effectively "erases" that object from existence, causing the entity to completely cease in function. It can stop certain inherent properties such as momentum, toxicity, and generally any effect it may impose on its surrounding. Disease, poison, and corruption can be completely negated.

Limitation: The magic to kill something with Zeitsterben requires Satanel to actually strike the target, so those physically above Satanel will be able to avoid them, no matter how many "deaths" he can see. It’s noted He can't kill anything that is out of his reach like mages that fly even though he has shown he be able to keep up and catch his air time. There are also existences that are hard or impossible to kill due to their nature. While it would be possible to see its deadlines, it would mean deciphering "advanced lines of death" levels higher than the normal Concept of Death. It’s stated gold Macht creates is also virtually indestructible and unmalleable; upon looking at their deadlines by Satanel, they possess way fewer then material from naturally occurring gold which forced him to concentrate to perceive their death. Something "made of words" and "which has yet to exist" cannot be "killed". Things that also can be called a "phenomenon" like "wind storms" and "typhoons", and while individual events of such phenomenon can be dispersed, it is impossible to outright kill the phenomenon itself from existence. Satanel has to concentrate harder to see death when his opponent uses way more complex spells because those way more layered spells possess a complexe death. He cannot kill anything which is yet to exist. It stated if Satanel was a human, his brain would’ve overheated immensely from perceiving the death of numerous complex spells at once. Satanel works off of the notion of killing what she perceives as alive, so while he claims to be able to kill God "as long as it's alive", he can do nothing to God because "God is not alive or dead" and later admitted it was a metaphor. His immense mana and physical abilities make him formidable, but his ability to perceive death and his ability to deliver it are two separate matters.

WEAPON
Reinhard: is Satanel’s signature massive longsword with a heavy double-edged blade, notched on both sides near the tip. In its dormant form, the pommel is a single spike, but after awakening, it splits open into several. The grip is plain, but the guard is skeletal, with a skull-design on each side leading to the rib cage from which the blade emerges; on one side of the blade, the skull is that of a human, while the other uses a horned demon screaming skull. Initially, the crossguard is folded in against the rich. Satanel uses this sword to trace deadlines.
